Package: lustless
Version: 0.1.0
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: LustLess Maintainers <maintainers@lustless.invalid>
Depends: libgtk-3-0, libayatana-appindicator3-1, libsqlcipher1, libsecret-1-0, systemd, policykit-1, dbus, iproute2, sqlite3, ca-certificates
Recommends: xfce4-indicator-plugin
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: Accountability client: screen accountability + DNS filtering (Linux edition)
 Clean-room Linux reimplementation of the Covenant Eyes "Victory Shield" 10.1.44
 behavior surface. Provides on-device screen accountability (capture plus a
 local classifier process — screenshot data never leaves the device),
 DNS-level web filtering with per-query verdicts via a local forwarder on
 127.0.0.2:53, a token-authenticated local dashboard, and a single
 polkit-gated, journald-audited administrative escape hatch.
 .
 This package ships the lustlessd system daemon, the lustless-classifier
 scoring process, the lustless-agent GTK tray helper, and the lustlessctl
 CLI. Supported desktop flavors: Zorin OS Lite 17 (Xfce), Zorin OS 17 Core
 (GNOME), Xubuntu 24.04 (Xfce), Ubuntu 24.04 (GNOME), and Lubuntu 24.04
 (LXQt), plus generic systemd Linux desktops. The tray needs an SNI host:
 xfce4-indicator-plugin on Xfce (Recommends), the AppIndicator GNOME
 extension on GNOME (Suggests; preinstalled-enabled on Ubuntu, declared for
 minimal GNOME installs), and none on LXQt, where the agent degrades to
 notifications with lustlessctl status and the local dashboard.
